Let me design the TDD approach for each thread:

**Thread 1 (BLOCKING XSS in app.js flowHtml token chip)** — RED test: source-level test in a new/existing test file asserting `site/factory/app.js`'s flowHtml token chip wraps the title value in `esc(`. But a raw source assertion is brittle. A better approach: extract the chip-building into a testable form? No — keep surgical. Actually, I could write the test to check that within the `flowHtml` function body, the `title="'` + is followed by `esc(`. Simplest robust assertion: read source, find the token-chip block (`if (s.tokens) {` in flowHtml), assert it contains `title="' +\n        esc(`. Hmm.

Alternative cleaner approach: add to test_factoryFlow.js a suite "factoryBoard app.js — XSS regression guards (source-level)" that reads the app.js source via file_read and asserts:
1. Every `'title="'` interpolation inside flowHtml is wrapped in esc — hard to do generically.

